82
00:02:43.190 --> 00:02:49.290
This episode aired on March 15th, 2012, and it was not a beloved episode.

83
00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:57.130
Sorry to say, in my deep diving of this episode, I just came across a lot of critique.

84
00:02:57.390 --> 00:03:00.390
Did you happen to read what Miles wrote about it?

85
00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:01.470
You know what?

86
00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:03.210
Miles was not even the harshest critic.

87
00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:04.150
You're kidding.

88
00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:05.510
Miles gave it a C+.

89
00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:07.810
Miles McNutt, C+.

90
00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:09.310
Who was the harshest critic?

91
00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:14.010
There was a critic named Matt Doherty who wrote for The Filtered Lens, and he gave it

92
00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:20.750
two out of ten stars and said that this episode was, quote, the worst, and that it, quote,

93
00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:23.090
lacked any form of logic or emotion.

94
00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:24.450
Oh, my God.

95
00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:25.410
I don't know.

96
00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:26.730
It was just like scathing.

97
00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:27.450
Oh, my God.

98
00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:28.170
Scathing review.

99
00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:30.710
That is really bad.

100
00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:31.630
I know.

101
00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:33.330
I'm sorry.

102
00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:35.710
That's what I'm saying.

103
00:03:35.710 --> 00:03:37.330
I didn't know how to not mention it.

104
00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:37.610
No, I know.

105
00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:43.890
Because it was all my research led me to these just like really, really harsh reviews.

106
00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:44.490
Oh, my gosh.

107
00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:44.850
Okay.

108
00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:49.930
It was also ranked 23 out of 24 in the Office Tally fan poll.

109
00:03:50.470 --> 00:03:52.790
It's going to get worse before it gets better.

110
00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:58.930
Matt Doherty also said, was anyone else rooting for Aaron to just stay in Florida?

111
00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:00.490
I certainly was.

112
00:04:01.390 --> 00:04:07.810
And a review from Click Clack said this episode was, quote, miserably insufferable, end quote.

113
00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:16.140
Yeah.

114
00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:17.500
Oh, my gosh.

115
00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:21.000
A lot of critics, however, praised Catherine Tate.

116
00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:25.440
They were very excited to see what she was going to bring to the show moving forward.

117
00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:29.120
People also praised the balloon cold open.

118
00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:34.640
And, you know, all that said, this episode was still the highest rated show on NBC the night it aired.

119
00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:36.900
So we have that.

120
00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:37.820
We have that.

121
00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:40.280
That's fast fact number one.

122
00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:40.600
Okay.

123
00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:42.080
Just a lot of bad news.

124
00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:43.960
Fast fact number one really tickled me.

125
00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:44.460
Okay.

126
00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:45.380
Moving on.

127
00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:48.840
Fast fact number two is an Office Ladies update.

128
00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:55.460
We want everyone out there to know we had an amazing show in Toronto at the Just for Laughs Festival.

129
00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:56.900
We kicked off the festival.

130
00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:58.720
Yes, we were opening night.

131
00:04:59.140 --> 00:04:59.940
Oh, my gosh.

132
00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:00.760
What a turnout.

133
00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:06.740
You guys, it is so fun to go on the road and see everybody and meet everyone.

134
00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:13.100
We did, like, an impromptu little meet and greet kind of after the show, and we got to meet a lot of people.

135
00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:13.880
We did.

136
00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:17.420
We didn't have a formal meet and greet for the show, but—

137
00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:18.800
There was a show right after us.

138
00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:19.220
So—

139
00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:20.260
They were kicking us out.

140
00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:20.460
Yeah.

141
00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:24.100
But we were like, we're going to take 15, 20 minutes.

142
00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:25.460
We went to the front of the stage.

143
00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:26.880
We signed as many things as we could.

144
00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.440
We took as many selfies as we could.

145
00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:36.600
But it was—I mean, we're always kind of doing our art in a vacuum where, you know, we do it, and then it goes on TV.

146
00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.620
Or we talk in our microphones, and then—

147
00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:40.560
In our closets or in a little room.

148
00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:40.840
Yeah.

149
00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:43.140
And we're like, oh, I guess maybe someone listened.

150
00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.440
So this was the joy of live performance.

151
00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:47.300
And I love our live show.

152
00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:48.100
Me too.

153
00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:51.300
And something really exciting happened, which is why I was bringing it up.

154
