And here's what Google Translate has to say.

197
00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:28.580
Ready?

198
00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:29.300
Mm-hmm.

199
00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:30.540
Syrup.

200
00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:32.420
Syrup.

201
00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:33.820
Syrup.

202
00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:36.960
It sounds like a combination of syrup and syrup.

203
00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:38.680
It sounds like syrup to me.

204
00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:39.880
I hear syrup.

205
00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:40.900
Hmm.

206
00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:41.460
Hmm.

207
00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:42.920
What are you doing?

208
00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:44.020
What are you doing today?

209
00:07:44.120 --> 00:07:44.920
What are you doing?

210
00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:46.600
This is our Laurel Yanni moment.

211
00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:48.680
Do you say syrup or syrup?

212
00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:49.860
What do you hear?

213
00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:56.680
I want you to know, I just Googled syrup, and did you know that there is an American pronunciation

214
00:07:57.500 --> 00:07:59.280
and a British pronunciation?

215
00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:01.440
Are you British, Jenna?

216
