Maybe I am.

217
00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:03.960
You tell me.

218
00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:04.820
Syrup.

219
00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:06.260
Syrup.

220
00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:07.460
Syrup.

221
00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:08.680
You're British.

222
00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:09.400
I'm British.

223
00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:10.500
Cassie, we're British!

224
00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:11.960
Sam, we're American!

225
00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:15.680
Moving on now to Fast Fact No.

226
00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:16.020
3.

227
00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:19.680
Angela, my favorite thing is when I take Fast Fact No.

228
00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:19.920
3.

229
00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:21.120
You have a Fast Fact No.

230
00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:21.900
3 for us.

231
00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:22.500
What do you got?

232
00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:28.140
You know, I was just curious about where all the office has been remade.

233
00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:29.060
Then I looked it up.

234
00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:35.500
Well, I know they just are about to launch one in Australia with a female boss, right?

235
00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:36.320
Okay.

236
00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:40.380
So, the new Australian version has gotten a lot of buzz online.

237
00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:42.640
It's in production right now.

238
00:08:42.820 --> 00:08:43.180
Okay.

239
00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:49.260
And obviously, we all know the OG version, which was created in the United Kingdom by Ricky Gervais

240
00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:53.320
and Stephen Merchant, but their idea has spread to all these other countries.

241
00:08:53.560 --> 00:09:01.200
There have been office remakes in Brazil, Canada, Chile, the Czech Republic, Finland, France,

242
00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:08.340
Germany, Greece, India, Israel, Poland, Saudi Arabia, Sweden, and of course, our version

243
00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:09.500
in the United States.

244
00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:12.060
And here's the thing I found really interesting.

245
00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:17.600
A lot of these remakes were starting right when our show started at the same time.

246
00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:18.180
Yeah.

247
00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:23.780
And they didn't run as long as ours did, but you can see all of their TV posters for their

248
00:09:23.780 --> 00:09:24.260
remakes.

249
00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:25.480
They're on IMDb.

250
00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:26.540
I can put them in stories.

251
00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:27.860
Isn't it true?

252
00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:33.840
I remember hearing this, that the France Jim and Pam were like gorgeous, like runway models.

253
00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:34.300
Yes.

254
00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:36.600
They were super, super beautiful.

255
00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:37.080
Yes.

256
00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:38.880
In fact, I'll tell you how they're described.

257
00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:39.320
Okay.

258
00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:44.600
The Jim-Pam characters are stunning and nubile up-and-comers.

259
00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:47.220
And then the article said, this is France after all.

260
00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:53.180
You know, we get asked all the time, there are always these rumors of another American

261
00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:58.840
version, like a reboot or a remake or a spinoff.

262
00:09:59.140 --> 00:09:59.420
Yeah.

263
00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:06.980
No one has ever in all of these years ever one time contacted me about being on another version

264
00:10:06.980 --> 00:10:08.520
of The Office or any cast member.

265
00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:11.640
Whenever I talk to the cast members, they're like, never heard anything.

266
00:10:11.780 --> 00:10:12.780
Not a word.

267
00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:16.100
And we get like tagged in all these articles all the time.

268
00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:19.300
